WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:07.300
Sarah Mardini faces up to 25 years in prison
for helping other refugees on the Greek island

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.610
of Lesbos
I would do it all over again for the rest

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.710
of my life.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.370
It’s transformed me from being a refugee
to a rescuer.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.640
She says she was volunteering with a rescue
team in Greece.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.960
On her way back to Germany from Greece, she
was arrested and charged with crimes including

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.800
people smuggling, money laundering and espionage.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.620
Amnesty International criticizes the case
as an attempt to criminalize humanitarian

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.790
work in a climate that is increasingly hostile
towards migrants and refugees

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:46.150
(The arrest) was shocking, draining.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.480
I was disappointed and heartbroken because
I was ready to leave.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:55.789
I was looking forward to studying again, and
someone just takes everything from you in

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.030
one second.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:04.860
Sarah spent 107 days in pre-trial detention
and was released on bail.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:11.319
She then returned to her college in Berlin
I never regret anything I have done and I

00:01:11.319 --> 00:01:16.369
know deep inside that I have done that because
I wanted to help people and that’s given

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:17.369
me motivation.

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:21.090
I didn’t do anything illegal because I didn’t
contact anyone directly.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.250
I was just on the shoreline, and our house,
the ERCI volunteer house, was just on the

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.250
shoreline.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.250
And I am just handing water and blankets.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.709
Do you think handing water and blankets is
illegal?

00:01:29.709 --> 00:01:31.389
No, it is not.

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:36.109
Interviewer: But people say, it is because
they know there is someone waiting, that is

00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:37.599
why they come.

00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:39.710
If they thought that there was no one.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:44.679
Sarah: I don’t believe that because when
I crossed there was no one waiting and I made

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:45.679
it.

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:49.009
And I knew there was no one waiting, in 2015.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:54.919
Sarah and her sister Yusra first made headlines
in 2015.

00:01:54.919 --> 00:01:59.979
After fleeing Syria, they used their swimming
skills to pull their boat to shore on its

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:03.090
journey from Turkey to Lesbos.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:15.569
They saved themselves and 18 other people
Yusra is now a UNHCR goodwill ambassador and

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:25.819
was on the refugee team at the Rio 2016 Olympics
Sarah won a scholarship to study social sciences

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:32.290
in Berlin but kept returning to Lesbos and
joined a Greek NGO that assists newly arrived

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.609
refugees .
I believe when you fear something, you should

00:02:35.609 --> 00:02:37.239
just go for it.

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:42.319
I fear the place that I landed in, and I wanted
to be on this ground again.

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:48.030
Following her arrest in August 2018 Sarah’s
classmates campaigned for her release

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.670
Florian BeckerDirector, Bard College Berlin
We are extremely relieved.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:55.519
It was just a beautiful moment to be able
to walk to our cafeteria with Sarah knowing

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:59.530
that everybody was going to be waiting there.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.370
But Greek authorities claim Sarah was part
of a criminal network.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:10.180
She is currently awaiting trial
The experience in general has given me this

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.269
traumatizing fear.

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:16.319
I am afraid I am not gonna get my freedom
back.

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:19.340
Because even if I am outside I am still under
trial.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.379
I still cannot go to the place that I love.

